      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Paris Observatory, founded in the 17th century, ranks among the world’s oldest astronomical observatories and sits in the 14th.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/15th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Until the early 1970s, the 14th housed chemical plants, electrical firms like Thomson, and Citroën’s car factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/15th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beneath the streets, the 14th’s catacombs echo with the city’s buried past, a chilling reminder of history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.parisinsidersguide.com/14th-arrondissement-paris.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early 20th‑century artists gathered at places like Villa Seurat, making the 14th a cultural hotspot of its era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.about-paris.com/14th-arrondissement.html",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
